update public.profiles set username = 'bea_bookbinder', display_name = 'Beatrix Lund', bio = 'I rebind paperbacks in linen. Cosy reads, classics, and long walks to the library.', pronouns = 'she/her', location = 'Copenhagen', accent = 'butter', profile_motif = 'botanical', favourite_genres = array['classics','romance','fantasy']::text[], favourite_authors = array['Jane Austen','Charlotte Brontë','Erin Morgenstern']::text[], reading_goal = 35, onboarded = true, created_at = '2025-08-18T09:56:54.980Z' where id = 'acd968b4-7d37-4bc2-bda2-10d7e078686c';






It''s a book about beauty as a moral alibi. Everyone is so clever and so cold and you want to sit at that table anyway. Henry remains the most dangerous man in fiction to have ever owned a pair of reading glasses.', false, true, 'public', '2026-09-26T13:56:18.980Z', '2026-09-26T13:56:18.980Z'),
  ('cdbd667a-cd64-4b26-9ea8-d41d6add1e6d', '5f54384a-ea71-406c-a187-412bf669f09a', '597dbe38-ae35-401c-9bca-9efe5aa824a7', 3.5, 'Shakespeare kids, unwell', 'Gorgeous premise, and the scenes where they speak in verse at the dinner table genuinely delighted me. But it wants so badly to be The Secret History that it forgets to be itself in the middle third. Still: the last act? Worth it.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-24T11:13:42.980Z', '2026-10-24T11:13:42.980Z'),
  ('8d661cb6-b3bf-4e51-be4a-06397e095a26', 'b105dbf5-10b2-43ef-b593-6a0b9a73d99d', 'e66bf754-65ea-4692-9c11-8dc2f964f081', 5, 'a witch, finally allowed to be bored, angry and free', 'Miller writes immortality as loneliness measured in centuries, and then lets Circe fill that time with herbs, pigs, lovers, a son. I loved that the climax is a choice rather than a battle. I want to plant a garden about it.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-11T11:16:42.980Z', '2026-10-11T11:16:42.980Z'),
  ('256b9079-6b0e-4dee-bb67-8239005debbf', 'b105dbf5-10b2-43ef-b593-6a0b9a73d99d', 'a5d2cc7c-ad31-436d-9c7e-f0ae2eb299cc', 4.5, null, 'The footnotes alone deserve a review. Kuang builds a magic system out of the gap between two words and then uses it to indict an entire empire. Robin''s arc made me furious in the right way. Ramy deserved better (we all know).', true, false, 'public', '2026-10-30T12:40:06.980Z', '2026-10-30T12:40:06.980Z'),
  ('c9e56200-2913-4a8a-9d59-2a07c4b19ad8', 'f290e8d0-65e6-45be-8b0c-4f7feeee92a1', 'fede530f-1d11-4a07-bf1f-7549f4189b12', 5, 'Peter''s chapters made me hold my breath', 'I didn''t know Rooney could write like this. Peter''s sections are clipped, jagged, almost unpunctuated — a man thinking faster than he can feel. Ivan''s are slow and literal and devastatingly sweet. It''s a book about grief that is mostly about tenderness, and I''m still a bit wrecked.', false, false, 'public', '2026-11-01T10:24:30.980Z', '2026-11-01T10:24:30.980Z'),
  ('1946b110-91b2-4f1e-b3e7-64b935a6859d', 'f290e8d0-65e6-45be-8b0c-4f7feeee92a1', '06262751-2db5-4dcf-97b9-58ead3f0e2f1', 4.5, null, '128 pages and not a wasted word. Bill Furlong''s decency is so ordinary and so costly. Read it in one sitting on the train back from Wexford and had to stare out the window for a while after.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-21T14:02:18.980Z', '2026-10-21T14:02:18.980Z'),
  ('898cfa30-5ccb-449b-a2d4-663e052c059f', '2a95913c-34a2-4cb1-823f-8bc5822b24d5', '45f06cf9-4d8d-482a-b0d7-ba7d47695289', 5, 'proposition 1: I have underlined all of it', 'Reading Bluets feels like eavesdropping on someone who is trying very hard to be honest. It''s philosophy, it''s heartbreak, it''s a list of every blue thing she''s ever loved. I bought a blue notebook immediately. I am a cliché and I''m at peace with it.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-14T13:19:06.980Z', '2026-10-14T13:19:06.980Z'),
  ('b995dc32-4509-4c34-9cfb-6ca861a4a4c1', '2a95913c-34a2-4cb1-823f-8bc5822b24d5', '1abf9a57-8de1-4a41-9977-c473ddd36c7f', 4.5, null, 'A novel written by a poet, which means some pages are so beautiful you have to put the book face down on your chest. The tobacco field chapters are among the best things I''ve read this year.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-03T10:04:06.980Z', '2026-10-03T10:04:06.980Z'),
  ('80f10eca-ab07-464f-91c0-4119b6e1bcfa', '1841d756-5b33-4b76-9f55-d4e86d91f5e0', '955cae93-d2f5-436b-b898-3d1eea828957', 4.5, 'the cat chapters are canon to me', 'Nakata talking to cats is the emotional centre of this book and nobody can tell me otherwise. The Kafka half is strange and occasionally frustrating, but the metaphysical storm stuff stayed with me for weeks. Best read in a small library while it rains.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-08T10:25:42.980Z', '2026-10-08T10:25:42.980Z'),
  ('8c1f1e61-af17-4299-9ff3-7f653aba77b2', '1841d756-5b33-4b76-9f55-d4e86d91f5e0', 'f7a44638-1088-4762-aedd-21386f98e9df', 4.5, null, 'Keiko is the most well-adjusted protagonist I''ve ever met and the world simply cannot handle it. Funny, eerie, and over in an afternoon. I now say "Irasshaimase!" in my head when I open the fridge.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-26T12:59:18.980Z', '2026-10-26T12:59:18.980Z'),
  ('580c5925-d043-4682-a5a7-4767788cf1c5', '3eca6936-a445-4846-badd-47eb4e0a2f5d', '1705590c-e6f1-41a7-b14e-20d761ef300a', 5, 'the green dress. that''s the review.', 'I picked this up expecting glamour and got a love story that made me sob on public transport. Evelyn is monstrous and magnificent and I would let her ruin my life. Celia St. James, you will always be famous.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-22T10:27:30.980Z', '2026-10-22T10:27:30.980Z'),
  ('afaa1472-9a4a-43bd-99e8-e550ad756a01', '3eca6936-a445-4846-badd-47eb4e0a2f5d', 'f6d6ee67-a698-435c-bf45-c86e7bfe29ac', 5, null, 'Third read. Still thought it might end differently this time. The last chapter is not a chapter, it''s a wound.', false, false, 'public', '2026-09-28T09:30:30.980Z', '2026-09-28T09:30:30.980Z'),
  ('793b107b-75e6-4a15-967b-158f2d46f71f', '5ec8a2e5-0d9d-40e9-81d0-61e5e3e0de4d', 'd16151ce-3f9d-4ef3-bdb1-7caee92f1231', 5, 'the house is not haunted, the house is lonely', 'Jackson understood that the scariest thing in a haunted house is the person who wants to stay. Eleanor''s longing to belong anywhere, even somewhere that wants to eat her, is the real ghost. The opening paragraph is perfect and I will die on this hill (house).', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-20T13:42:48.980Z', '2026-10-20T13:42:48.980Z'),
  ('ab8fce26-0ff7-4704-9251-f4c4dc7f78cc', '5ec8a2e5-0d9d-40e9-81d0-61e5e3e0de4d', 'e0d46716-8e06-41c1-8d2a-604796eca08b', 4, null, 'This book is a sugar-glazed nightmare. The Bunnies'' dialogue is so funny it hurts and then suddenly it''s body horror. Not for everyone. Absolutely for me.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-25T13:21:48.980Z', '2026-10-25T13:21:48.980Z'),
  ('cd3aa472-36ef-4f7f-92a1-cf36832dc496', '61772e2e-fe1a-4c4e-a610-af2629180030', '319cd7bf-5890-48e7-80fc-d4ecf9f47f59', 2.5, 'DNF at page 310, respectfully', 'I get it. I get why it''s important. But I don''t need four pages of internal monologue every time someone raises an eyebrow. Will watch the films instead and feel only slightly guilty. The sandworms are great though.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-17T12:54:30.980Z', '2026-10-17T12:54:30.980Z'),
  ('ad40223d-deb2-44e6-a131-b9c52904915b', '61772e2e-fe1a-4c4e-a610-af2629180030', '1f673cdf-1a23-4068-8e67-02e58c2e99df', 4, null, 'Is it literature? No. Did I read it in two days with my heart rate up the entire time? Yes. Tairn is the best character and he''s a dragon who is mostly annoyed.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-07T13:50:54.980Z', '2026-10-07T13:50:54.980Z'),
  ('8204ba75-0a95-4c00-aa22-3684a0197f05', '11f2e717-7b9b-4abd-a567-6a7de501fdab', '96c82f65-6dda-4479-ac5b-e253e90c3d25', 5, '"history has failed us, but no matter"', 'Min Jin Lee lets time move like weather over this family. No one is a hero, everyone is trying. Sunja is one of the great literary mothers. I read the last section twice.', false, false, 'public', '2026-09-22T12:47:18.980Z', '2026-09-22T12:47:18.980Z'),
  ('45da75f3-5e95-4f44-841c-b6ece8b2edcf', '11f2e717-7b9b-4abd-a567-6a7de501fdab', 'fc5fa64a-d839-402a-9ef9-122c3704b294', 4.5, null, 'Butler wastes no time on the mechanics of the time travel because the point isn''t how — it''s what it does to Dana to keep surviving. Terrifying, clear-eyed, essential.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-15T09:40:06.980Z', '2026-10-15T09:40:06.980Z'),
  ('face306b-88f5-4145-9384-d3e62eff3242', 'acd968b4-7d37-4bc2-bda2-10d7e078686c', '6dea3f39-b22e-4346-81e9-3dfc3df54cd4', 4.5, 'a book to read by candlelight', 'The plot is gossamer, but who cares when the tents are this beautiful? I want to live in the Ice Garden. I want a scarf in exactly that shade of red. Perfect for a November weekend.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-05T12:08:36.980Z', '2026-10-05T12:08:36.980Z'),
  ('8407d791-2ed4-4f47-92b2-104b7a0175eb', 'acd968b4-7d37-4bc2-bda2-10d7e078686c', '9cb6880e-10ae-4805-afaa-d721fc295c3b', 4.5, null, 'I read this slowly, one hall a night. It made me want to be kinder to birds and more curious about statues. The reveal is clever but the real joy is Piranesi himself — the gentlest narrator I''ve met.', false, false, 'public', '2026-10-13T13:01:06.980Z', '2026-10-13T13:01:06.980Z');









